    "content" : "Here&#39;s some photos of the circuit board I&#39;m making for the Automatic Garden Waterer project. I have screw terminals on the side for +5V power and ground along with a chip socket for the ATMEGA328P. There&#39;s also a 16 pin female header that the 16x2 character LCD display plugs into and a trimpot at the top to adjust the contrast. The resistor along the side is used to pull the uC reset pin high and will have a push button added to it so it can be reset. The LCD is not displaying anything because I don&#39;t have any 16MHz crystals at the moment but they&#39;re coming in the mail. I did jumper wire in the crystal from the Arduino board and it worked as I expected. All that is left to do is wire up the buttons and output for the relay and then figure out how to mount it to the lid. ",
    "objectType" : "note",
    "originalContent" : "Here's some photos of the circuit board I'm making for the Automatic Garden Waterer project. I have screw terminals on the side for +5V power and ground along with a chip socket for the ATMEGA328P. There's also a 16 pin female header that the 16x2 character LCD display plugs into and a trimpot at the top to adjust the contrast. The resistor along the side is used to pull the uC reset pin high and will have a push button added to it so it can be reset. The LCD is not displaying anything because I don't have any 16MHz crystals at the moment but they're coming in the mail. I did jumper wire in the crystal from the Arduino board and it worked as I expected. All that is left to do is wire up the buttons and output for the relay and then figure out how to mount it to the lid. ",
